      en: "Yinxu in Anyang, Henan province, is the ruins of the late Shang dynasty (c. 1300–1046 BCE). Discovered in 1899, it is one of China's most important archaeological sites. The site includes palaces, royal tombs, and workshops. Of particular significance are the oracle bones, which bear the earliest known form of Chinese writing. Yinxu was declared a UNESCO World Heritage site in 2006. Excavations have unearthed over 150,000 oracle bones. Yinxu provides unique insights into China's Bronze Age and Shang society.",
