      en: "Mukden Palace in Shenyang, Liaoning province, was the imperial palace of the early Qing dynasty before the court moved to Beijing. Built in 1625 by Nurhaci and expanded by his son Hong Taiji, the palace blends Manchu and Chinese architectural styles. It comprises over 300 rooms and 70 buildings. Mukden Palace served as the political center during the Manchu conquest of China. In 1987, it was declared a UNESCO World Heritage site as an extension of the Forbidden City. It is a key symbol of Manchu history.",
