      en: "Zhenyuan Ancient Town in Guizhou is renowned for its fusion of Han Chinese and Miao ethnic cultures. Situated along the Wu River, it was a crucial stop on the ancient Tea Horse Road. Architecture features wooden houses with extended eaves. The Qinglong Cave complex includes temples and pavilions built into cliffs. With over 2,000 years of history, Zhenyuan became a protected historical site in 1986. Local crafts include embroidery and batik. Boat tours on the Wu River offer scenic views of the town's riverside buildings.",
