      en: "Taierzhuang Ancient Town in Shandong province is famed for the 1938 Battle of Taierzhuang during the Second Sino-Japanese War. The town has over 2,000 years of history. Located along the Grand Canal, it was a key commercial port. Its architecture blends northern and southern Chinese styles. The town was heavily damaged in the battle but later rebuilt. Now a tourist attraction with restored buildings and a museum, the battle was China's first major victory in the war. The town is also known for local snacks. Reconstruction started in 2008.",
